"g001|Pocket Gravity Well|Hyper-casual / Physics|js|drag|neon|Drag to drop temporary gravity wells that bend a falling orb into a cup of coins.|Each level gives you three wells, one orb and a coin cluster. You place wells before releasing, then watch physics do the rest.|Wells expire on a timer, so you are not building a path — you are choreographing a sequence of pulls in the right order.|Endless: level generator rolls well-count, gravity strength, obstacle layout and coin scatter from a seed. A daily seed is shared by everyone.|Watching a plan unfold without being able to touch it creates a tiny suspense arc every twelve seconds.|physics,one-touch,planning,seeded-levels",

"g002|One Tile Deeper|Puzzle / Digging|js|swipe|duotone|Swipe to dig down one tile. Every tile you remove makes the ones above fall.|Dig toward treasure while the ceiling collapses behind you. You can only move down, left or right, never back up.|The collapse is deterministic and previewed as a faint outline, so it is a planning game wearing a panic costume.|Infinite: depth is endless, generated in chunks with escalating cave density and rare treasure rooms.|The preview line makes failure feel like your own arithmetic error, which is the most forgivable kind of loss.|puzzle,digging,procedural,one-touch",

