"g061|Cipher Kitchen|Puzzle / Language|js|typing|clay|Recipes are written in a substitution cipher. Decode them to cook.|Each recipe uses a cipher. Decode ingredient names, then cook in the right order.|The cipher gets harder (Caesar, then Vigenere, then homophonic) as you progress through cuisines.|Endless recipes with a cipher difficulty ladder and a cuisine progression.|Learning real cryptography while cooking is a genuinely novel combination.|puzzle,ciphers,learning,levels",

"g062|Sokoban Sushi|Puzzle / Push|js|swipe|pixel32|Push sushi pieces into bento boxes. The pieces are the boxes.|Every piece is both cargo and container, so moving one changes what the others can do.|The dual role of each object makes classic push puzzles much richer.|Generated grids with piece counts, box layouts and solver verification.|Dual-purpose objects are a cheap way to multiply puzzle depth.|puzzle,sokoban,food,levels",

"g063|Letter Ladder|Puzzle / Words|js|typing|paper|Change one letter at a time to climb from one word to another.|Each rung must be a real word. Longer ladders score more, and rare words score bonus.|The ladder is scored by word rarity, so vocabulary depth is the progression system.|Endless word pairs with difficulty by ladder length and a daily pair.|Vocabulary as a progression currency is elegant and endlessly extensible.|puzzle,words,vocabulary,daily",

"g064|Reverse Puzzle|Puzzle / Logic|js|tap|terminal|You start solved. Undo the solution to reach the scrambled state.|Every level is presented in its solved form and you must work backwards to create the puzzle.|Thinking backwards is a genuinely different cognitive mode and it makes familiar puzzles feel new.|Generated puzzles with forward-solvability guarantees and backward difficulty rating.|Inverting the direction of play is a simple change with profound effects on how puzzles feel.|puzzle,reverse,logic,levels",

"g065|Mirror Twin|Puzzle / Coordination|js|twoThumb|vector|Control two characters with mirrored inputs. What moves one moves the other in reverse.|Both characters must reach their exits. Walls are arranged so one path is the other's obstacle.|Mirrored control means you must think in symmetry, which is a skill the game teaches from scratch.|Generated levels with mirrored geometry and solver-verified solutions.|One input controlling two bodies is a coordination puzzle with no learning curve.|puzzle,coordination,levels,two-thumb",

"g066|Weight Logic|Puzzle / Physics|js|drag|mono|Balance a scale using weights whose values you must deduce.|You are given unlabelled weights. Through a series of weighings, deduce each value and hit the target.|The game is a measurement puzzle: each weighing is an experiment you design.|Endless measurement puzzles with target sums and hidden weight sets.|Scientific method as a game loop is rare and intellectually satisfying.|puzzle,logic,measurement,levels",

"g067|Colorblind Proof|Puzzle / Pattern|js|tap|duotone|Puzzles where colour is never the answer, only pattern, shape and position.|Every puzzle is designed to be solvable without colour vision, using texture and geometry instead.|Accessibility is the design constraint that generates the originality, not an afterthought.|Endless generated puzzles with pattern grammars and difficulty tiers.|Designing for the constraint produces puzzles nobody else has built.|puzzle,accessibility,pattern,levels",

"g068|Time Rewind Puzzle|Puzzle / Time|js|drag|neon|Record your moves, then replay them alongside your new self.|Each level gives you a limited recording length. Solve the puzzle by cooperating with your past self.|Your past self is a physical object that can hold switches and block paths.|Generated levels requiring two or three simultaneous selves, solver-verified.|Cooperation with your own recorded past is a mechanic that stays interesting for hundreds of levels.|puzzle,time,record,levels",

"g069|Traffic Jam City|Puzzle / Routing|js|drag|isometric|Untangle a traffic jam by moving cars in the only order that works.|Tap cars to send them forward; they stop if blocked. Clear the intersection without gridlock.|The order of departures is the whole puzzle, and a wrong order creates a deadlock you must undo.|Endless intersections with new car counts, turn rules and deadlock detection.|Deadlock is a failure state players understand immediately, which makes retries frictionless.|puzzle,traffic,routing,levels",

"g070|Pipe Dream Redux|Puzzle / Pipes|js|tap|vector|Rotate pipes to connect a source to every outlet before the water arrives.|Water flows in real time. You have until it reaches each junction to complete that section.|Real-time flow turns a static routing puzzle into a race you can partially lose without losing entirely.|Endless boards with generated pipe inventories and flow timings.|Partial failure is a generous design that keeps players in the puzzle longer.|puzzle,pipes,real-time,endless",

"g071|Battery Balance|Puzzle / Energy|js|drag|terminal|Route power from batteries to devices, but every device has a minimum and maximum voltage.|Adjust transformers and routes so no device is under or over powered.|Overpowering is as bad as underpowering, so the solution is a narrow band rather than a maximum.|Endless circuits with device requirements and transformer inventories.|A two-sided constraint is much more interesting than a simple threshold.|puzzle,energy,routing,levels",

"g072|Lockpick Logic|Puzzle / Deduction|js|drag|ink|Deduce a combination from feedback, but you only get five attempts per lock.|Each attempt tells you how many digits are correct and how many are in the right place. Deduce the code.|Five attempts means the puzzle is about information design, not guessing.|Endless locks with generated codes and a difficulty ladder based on digit count and feedback quality.|Mastermind-style deduction with a hard attempt limit is tense and elegant.|puzzle,deduction,logic,levels",

"g073|Origami Unfold|Puzzle / Spatial|js|tap|paper|Unfold a paper shape one crease at a time to reveal a picture.|Each tap unfolds one crease. The picture is only visible when you unfold in the right order.|Folding order matters because the picture is on both sides of the paper.|Endless shapes with generated crease patterns and reveal images.|The reveal is the reward, so the game has a natural narrative beat every level.|puzzle,origami,spatial,levels",

"g074|Ant Farm Logic|Puzzle / Simulation|js|drag|clay|Draw pheromone trails and watch ants decide whether to follow.|Ants follow trails but deposit their own, so your instructions mutate as they are used.|You are programming with a medium that rewrites itself, which is a genuinely unusual puzzle mechanic.|Endless colonies with food layouts, obstacles and trail budgets.|Emergent behaviour from simple rules makes every solution feel alive.|puzzle,simulation,emergence,levels",

"g075|Laser Bounce Deluxe|Puzzle / Light|js|drag|neon|One laser, many mirrors, one target, and mirrors you can only use once.|Each mirror can be moved exactly once per level. Plan the whole path before you touch anything.|Limited moves on a continuous problem makes the puzzle about commitment rather than fiddling.|Generated rooms with mirror counts, target positions and move budgets.|Limiting moves on a continuous puzzle is a great difficulty lever.|puzzle,light,commitment,levels",

"g076|Ice Block Melt|Puzzle / Temperature|js|hold|watercolor|Hold to apply heat and melt an ice block. The water has to go somewhere.|Melt ice to reshape it, but melted water flows and refreezes in new places.|Refreezing is a tool, not a mistake, so the level is about cycles of melt and freeze.|Endless puzzles with ice shapes, drainage paths and target forms.|Phase change as a puzzle mechanic is visually beautiful and mechanically rich.|puzzle,physics,phase,levels",

"g077|Tile Flip Frenzy|Puzzle / Logic|js|tap|duotone|Tapping a tile flips it and every tile touching it. Make them all match.|Classic flip logic with a twist: tiles have three states instead of two.|Three states means parity tricks do not work, so players must actually solve the board.|Generated boards with state counts, sizes and solver-verified minimum moves.|Three-state flip puzzles are meaningfully harder than two-state and rarely seen.|puzzle,logic,tiles,levels",

"g078|Pressure Plate Path|Puzzle / Weight|js|drag|mono|Place weights on plates to open doors, but you must carry the weights with you.|Plates need a specific weight. You carry a limited set, so each door costs you future options.|Resource management inside a puzzle means later doors can be locked out by earlier choices.|Generated dungeons with plate requirements and weight inventories.|Puzzle resource management creates a real sense of consequence.|puzzle,weights,dungeon,levels",

"g079|Conveyor Chaos|Puzzle / Routing|js|drag|isometric|Route items on conveyor belts to the right machines without jamming.|Place and rotate belts. Items arrive continuously, so mistakes cascade into blockages.|Continuous flow means the puzzle cannot be paused — you fix jams as they happen.|Endless factories with item mixes, machine requirements and throughput goals.|Real-time routing with jams is a great fit for short mobile sessions.|puzzle,routing,real-time,levels",

"g080|Magnetic Sudoku|Puzzle / Numbers|js|drag|neon|Sudoku where some cells repel each other and cannot share a row.|Magnets in cells push numbers away. The magnetic rules replace some of the classic constraints.|Magnetic repulsion adds spatial reasoning to a pure logic puzzle.|Generated grids with magnet placements and solver verification.|Hybridising two rule systems creates puzzles neither system could produce alone.|puzzle,numbers,magnets,levels",

"g081|Word Snake Sudoku|Puzzle / Hybrid|js|swipe|paper|A word snake moves through a grid, and the letters it eats must form valid words.|Steer the snake to spell words in order. The grid refills with new letters.|The snake's body is the word, so a bad letter is a physical obstacle until you use it.|Endless grids with letter distributions and word-list difficulty tiers.|Making spelling physical is a great way to make a word game feel like a game.|puzzle,words,snake,levels",

"g082|Bottle Ship Logic|Puzzle / Packing|js|drag|clay|Fit oddly shaped objects into a bottle through a narrow neck.|Objects must be rotated and sequenced. The neck limits what can go in and when.|Packing order matters because some objects only fit if others go first.|Endless bottles with shape sets and capacity goals.|Packing puzzles are intuitive, tactile and almost entirely absent from mobile stores.|puzzle,packing,spatial,levels",

"g083|Gravity Puzzle Rooms|Puzzle / Gravity|js|tap|vector|Tap to rotate gravity ninety degrees and the whole room falls with you.|Rooms are full of loose objects. Rotating gravity moves everything, including the things you need.|Rotating gravity is both your movement and the puzzle's main source of chaos.|Generated rooms with object layouts, hazards and rotation budgets.|One-tap gravity rotation is a beautifully simple verb with enormous consequence.|puzzle,gravity,levels,tap",

"g084|Silhouette City|Creative / Puzzle|js|drag|duotone|Build a skyline from blocks so its shadow matches a target shape.|Place buildings of varying heights. The shadow is cast by a low sun, so height and position both matter.|Shadow matching inverts the usual building game: you build for the outline, not the object.|Endless targets with sun angles, building inventories and difficulty tiers.|Building for a shadow is a fresh constraint on a familiar creative verb.|creative,puzzle,shadow,levels",

"g085|Chain Link Logic|Puzzle / Counting|js|tap|mono|Link nodes so that each node's connection count equals its number.|Every node displays the number of links it needs. Connect them without exceeding any node's limit.|Local constraints create global puzzles, and dead ends are visible before you commit.|Generated graphs with degree sequences and guaranteed solutions.|Degree-constrained graphs are a rich puzzle space that mobile has barely touched.|puzzle,graphs,logic,levels",

"g086|Recipe Deduction|Puzzle / Deduction|js|typing|clay|You taste a dish and must deduce its ingredients from a pantry of possibilities.|Each level gives you a dish and feedback. Narrow down the recipe through deduction.|Feedback is qualitative (too salty, missing acid) so players learn to reason about flavour, not numbers.|Endless dishes with ingredient pools and a difficulty ladder by pool size.|Turning taste into a deduction system is genuinely original and teaches real cooking intuition.|puzzle,deduction,cooking,levels",

"g087|Reflection Maze|Puzzle / Light|js|drag|duotone|Navigate a beam of light through a maze by placing reflective walls.|You do not control the beam; you control the mirrors it will hit. Each placement changes the whole path.|The beam's path is continuous, so every change has global consequences.|Generated mazes with mirror inventories and target crystals.|Global consequence from local edits is the heart of a great puzzle.|puzzle,light,maze,levels",

"g088|Digit Drop|Puzzle / Math|js|drag|terminal|Drop digits into a grid to form valid equations in every row and column.|Numbers fall like Tetris pieces, but the goal is arithmetic, not lines.|Equations must be valid in both directions, so placement has two simultaneous constraints.|Endless grids with digit pools and equation difficulty tiers.|Dual constraints make a maths puzzle feel like a spatial puzzle.|puzzle,math,grid,levels",

"g089|Alien Language Decode|Puzzle / Language|js|tap|ink|Decode an alien script using only context and repetition.|You are given a corpus of alien text and pictures. Build a translation by inference.|No dictionary is given, so the player is doing real decipherment, and progress feels earned.|Endless corpora with generated grammars and difficulty by corpus size.|Real decipherment is a fantasy most players have never been able to act on.|puzzle,language,deduction,levels",

"g090|Gear Ratio Puzzle|Puzzle / Mechanics|js|drag|paper|Set a gear train so the output turns exactly once when the input turns seven times.|Choose and place gears to hit an exact ratio. Wrong ratios are visible but not obviously fixable.|Ratio arithmetic becomes a spatial puzzle, and both halves must be right.|Generated mechanisms with ratio targets and gear inventories.|Exact targets make mechanical puzzles satisfyingly deterministic.|puzzle,gears,math,levels",

"g091|Knot Untangle|Puzzle / Topology|js|drag|vector|Untangle a knot by moving crossings, not by pulling ends.|You can only move the crossing points. The knot must end up with no crossings at all.|Topology constraints mean the obvious moves often make things worse.|Generated knots with crossing counts and difficulty by knot complexity.|Topological puzzles are visually beautiful and mechanically unusual.|puzzle,topology,levels,drag",

"g092|Star Chart Connect|Puzzle / Space|js|drag|neon|Connect stars to form the constellation shown in a myth, but the myth is told in riddles.|Each level describes a constellation in words. You must work out which stars form it.|The riddle layer means the puzzle is partly interpretive, not purely geometric.|Endless constellations with generated star fields and riddle difficulty tiers.|Combining poetry with geometry is a rare and memorable pairing.|puzzle,space,riddles,levels",

"g093|Balance Beam Logic|Puzzle / Physics|js|drag|mono|Place weights on a beam so it balances, but you cannot see the weights' values.|Weights are visually different sizes but sizes lie. You must deduce values through balance experiments.|Every placement is an experiment, and the beam is the readout.|Endless balance puzzles with hidden weight sets and target configurations.|Turning a physics object into a measurement instrument is elegant.|puzzle,physics,measurement,levels",

"g094|Room Resize|Puzzle / Space|js|drag|isometric|Stretch and shrink rooms to make objects fit through doorways.|Rooms can be resized along their axes. Objects have fixed sizes, so the level geometry must change.|Resizing is global, so making one doorway passable can make another impossible.|Generated layouts with resize budgets and solver verification.|Non-Euclidean-feeling space manipulation is a striking puzzle idea.|puzzle,space,levels,drag",

"g095|Optical Path|Puzzle / Optics|js|drag|neon|Route light through prisms to split it into the exact colours a target needs.|White light enters, prisms split it, and each colour must reach a different receptor.|Splitting means one beam becomes many, so the puzzle's complexity grows geometrically.|Generated optical benches with prism inventories and colour targets.|Colour as a puzzle dimension is beautiful and underused.|puzzle,light,colour,levels",

"g096|Sequence Sleuth|Puzzle / Patterns|js|tap|terminal|Find the rule behind a sequence, then predict the next five terms.|Each level shows a sequence. You propose the rule; the game tests it against hidden terms.|You are graded on the rule, not the answer, so guessing is useless.|Endless sequences from a rule grammar with difficulty by rule depth.|Rewarding the rule rather than the answer is a genuinely better puzzle design.|puzzle,patterns,math,levels",

"g097|Fuse Box Fix|Puzzle / Circuits|js|drag|terminal|Restore power to a building by replacing fuses without overloading any circuit.|Each fuse has an amperage. Devices need specific currents, and the total must never exceed the mains limit.|The global limit makes the puzzle about allocation rather than connection.|Endless buildings with device loads, fuse inventories and mains limits.|A single global constraint turns a wiring puzzle into a resource puzzle.|puzzle,circuits,allocation,levels",

"g098|Puzzle Painting|Creative / Puzzle|js|drag|watercolor|Paint a canvas using only the colours the palette allows, matching a target image.|Each brush stroke is a limited resource. You must plan the painting in layers.|The palette limitation means the puzzle is about colour mixing, not drawing skill.|Endless target images with generated palettes and stroke budgets.|Art-making as a puzzle is a category almost nobody has built for mobile.|creative,puzzle,art,levels",

"g099|Number Nest|Puzzle / Math|js|drag|vector|Nest numbers inside each other so that each outer number equals the sum of its contents.|Build nested structures that satisfy arithmetic at every level.|Recursion as a puzzle mechanic is unusual and scales to real depth.|Generated targets with nesting depth and number inventories.|Recursive arithmetic is a beautiful puzzle space with almost no competition.|puzzle,math,recursion,levels",

"g100|Final Boss Logic|Puzzle / Meta|js|tap|ink|Every hundred levels, the game hands you a puzzle made of the rules you have learned, with no hints.|A boss level combines mechanics from every previous world into one multi-stage puzzle.|The boss has no new mechanics, only new combinations, so it tests mastery rather than novelty.|Endless: boss every hundred levels, generated from the mechanics you have unlocked so far.|Periodic mastery tests give a long game a rhythm and a sense of graduation.|puzzle,meta,boss,levels"

