"g167|Lamp Workshop|Merge / Light|js|drag|neon|Merge filaments and shades into lamps whose light reveals hidden things in the room.|Each lamp combination casts a different quality of light. Certain objects only appear under specific lamps.|Light quality as a puzzle key makes the merge tree functionally meaningful.|Endless rooms with hidden objects and lamp requirements.|Making the merge output a perception tool rather than a number is excellent design.|merge,light,puzzle,discovery",
"g168|Soap Alchemy|Merge / Chemistry|js|drag|pastel|Merge oils and lye into soaps with properties that affect how the whole board behaves.|Soap bars act as tools: some lubricate the board, some harden tiles, some dissolve them.|The merge output changes the board's rules, so merging is also terraforming.|Endless recipes with new reagents and board modifiers.|Merging into board modifiers is a mechanically rich twist on the genre.|merge,chemistry,systems,levels",
"g169|Ink & Quill|Merge / Writing|js|drag|ink|Merge words into sentences, sentences into paragraphs, paragraphs into a story that is then illustrated.|Each merge produces a larger unit of writing. The final story is generated from your merges.|The game turns writing into a merge tree and the output is genuinely readable.|Endless genres with new narrative grammars and illustration styles.|Producing a real story as the output of a merge game is a remarkable idea.|merge,writing,narrative,generated",
"g170|Puppet Workshop|Merge / Craft|js|drag|paper|Merge joints, heads and costumes into puppets that then perform the show you assemble.|Build puppets by merging parts, then stage a scene with them. The show is scored on coherence.|Performance is the validation step, so crafting has a purpose beyond collection.|Endless plays with new character parts and stage requirements.|Crafting that ends in a performance gives a merge game a natural climax.|merge,craft,performance,theatre",
"g171|Kite Maker|Merge / Craft|js|drag|watercolor|Merge spars and sails into kites, then fly them in wind you cannot change.|Build a kite from merged parts, then test it against the day's wind. Design determines flight.|Wind conditions vary by day, so a kite that failed yesterday may fly today.|Endless days with generated wind profiles and kite festivals.|Designing for uncontrollable conditions is a lovely source of variety.|merge,craft,wind,testing",
"g172|Boat Builder|Merge / Craft|js|drag|lowpoly|Merge planks and hulls into boats, then launch them into water that judges your seams.|Combine parts into vessels. Watertightness depends on how the parts were merged.|Leaks are visible and progressive, so design failures are dramatic and educational.|Endless waters with new conditions and vessel requirements.|Visible failure in a craft game makes iteration genuinely exciting.|merge,craft,physics,testing",
"g173|Candy Geology|Merge / Science|js|drag|pastel|Merge candy layers into rock strata, then read the geological history you just created.|Each merge compresses layers. The resulting strata tell a story you can interpret.|The game teaches stratigraphy by making you the one who deposits it.|Endless formations with new materials and interpretive goals.|Making a science lesson out of candy is a delightful and original combination.|merge,science,education,layers",
"g174|Sand Sculptor|Merge / Art|js|drag|watercolor|Merge wet sand into shapes, and shapes into a sculpture that erodes while you work.|Combine sand into forms. The sculpture's detail level depends on the merges you chose.|Erosion means the piece is degrading as it is built, so efficiency matters.|Endless festivals with new subjects and tide schedules.|Building against decay gives a cosy game real stakes.|merge,art,decay,creative",
"g175|Glassblower|Merge / Craft|js|drag|neon|Merge molten gathers into vessels, and the shape is decided by how you merged them.|Combine glass blobs and shape them with breath and rotation. Cooling locks the shape permanently.|Cooling is a deadline, so the final decision must be made before the glass sets.|Endless commissions with new vessel requirements and colour recipes.|A permanent cooling deadline gives a craft game genuine tension.|merge,craft,deadline,glass",
"g176|Lock & Key Merge|Merge / Puzzle|js|drag|ink|Merge keys to open locks, and merge locks to seal doors that should stay sealed.|Keys and locks are both mergeable. A key merged too far will not fit the lock it was made for.|Merging past the useful tier is a real and recoverable mistake, which is a lovely design space.|Endless vaults with new lock grammars and key tiers.|Over-merging as a failure mode is a clever twist on the genre.|merge,puzzle,keys,levels",
