"g183|Terrarium Builder|Merge / Collection|js|drag|watercolor|Merge mosses and stones into a terrarium that slowly tells you whether it is happy.|Combine elements into layers. Humidity, light and drainage determine survival.|The terrarium's health is visible as condensation and colour, so feedback is aesthetic rather than numeric.|Endless plants with new requirements and container shapes.|Aesthetic feedback for a hidden simulation is elegant and relaxing.|merge,zen,simulation,nature",
"g184|Bee Hotel|Merge / Collection|js|drag|pastel|Merge nesting tubes to attract solitary bees, each with a different personality and schedule.|Combine tube sizes and materials to attract species. Different bees emerge at different times.|The hotel is a calendar as much as a collection, so timing matters.|Endless seasons with new bee species and flowering calendars.|A collection game about hospitality rather than acquisition is quietly lovely.|merge,collection,nature,hospitality",
