"g352|Hot Potato Phones|Party / Local|js|shake|neon|Everyone holds a corner of the screen. The bomb goes to whoever is holding still.|Multi-touch detects who is touching. The bomb transfers and eventually detonates on one person.|Multi-touch as a party mechanic is clever and physical.|Endless rounds with new rules.|Using multi-touch for a party game is a genuinely smart use of a phone.|party,local-multiplayer,physical,comedy",
"g353|Whisper Draw|Party / Local|js|drag|paper|Telephone game with drawing: someone draws, the next person describes, the next draws the description.|Pass the phone. Each stage transforms the previous one. The final comparison is the payoff.|The classic format with a digital twist and automatic comparison.|Endless rounds and player counts.|A proven party format, digitised with automatic reveal.|party,drawing,local-multiplayer,comedy",
"g354|One Phone Trivia|Party / Local|js|tap|neon|Trivia where the phone is passed and everyone answers in secret on the same device.|Each player answers privately by passing the phone, then all answers are revealed together.|Secret input on a shared device creates suspense and accusations.|Endless question sets with new reveal formats.|Secret input on one device is a clever and underused party mechanic.|party,trivia,local-multiplayer,social",
"g355|Local Vote|Party / Local|js|tap|clay|Everyone votes on a question, and the results are revealed only after all votes are in.|Pass the phone, vote in secret, then see the split. Arguments follow.|The reveal is the entire game, and it is endlessly replayable with any group.|Endless question packs and voting formats.|The reveal moment is the product, and it costs almost nothing to make.|party,voting,local-multiplayer,social",
