"g379|Spy Among Us|Party / Local|js|tap|duotone|Everyone gets a word except one player, who must bluff their way through.|Pass the phone to reveal roles. Then describe the word without saying it, and find the spy.|A classic social deduction format, streamlined for one device.|Endless word sets and role variations.|One-device social deduction is a proven and highly replayable party game.|party,social,deduction,local-multiplayer",
"g380|Negotiation Table|Party / Local|js|tap|clay|Four players, one finite resource, and everyone needs more than exists.|Players negotiate allocations face to face, then submit agreements the app enforces.|The app enforces deals so promises are binding, which changes social dynamics completely.|Endless scenarios with new resources and incentives.|Making agreements enforceable is a genuinely new mechanic for party games.|party,negotiation,strategy,local-multiplayer",
"g381|Trade Table|Party / Local|js|tap|isometric|Everyone has goods and needs. Trade face to face, and the app tracks the economy.|Players trade resources. Prices emerge from player behaviour rather than design.|Emergent player-driven economies in a party setting are fascinating to watch.|Endless resource sets and market rules.|Emergent economics in a party game is a rich and rare design.|party,economics,trading,local-multiplayer",
"g382|Party Auction|Party / Local|js|tap|neon|Everyone bids for advantages, and the currency is the fun you have already had.|Bidding with points earned earlier creates a natural catch-up mechanic.|Making past fun into currency is a clever and self-aware economy.|Endless auction rounds with new lots.|A self-referential economy keeps a party game balanced and funny.|party,auction,strategy,local-multiplayer",
