"g401|Deck of Small Things|Deckbuilder / Strategy|js|drag|paper|Your deck is made of ordinary objects: a key, a bus ticket, a boiled sweet.|Each card is a mundane item with a specific, limited effect. You build a deck from what you find.|Power fantasy is replaced by resourcefulness, which makes every card feel earned.|Endless runs with new item sets and encounter types.|A deckbuilder about ordinary objects is a genuinely fresh thematic space.|deckbuilder,strategy,roguelike,levels",
"g402|Tower of Bad Ideas|Tower Defense / Comedy|js|drag|clay|Your towers are terrible ideas, and they work anyway.|Place absurd towers with unintended effects. A tower of stacked chairs blocks a path but falls over sometimes.|Deliberately unreliable towers make defence a comedy of errors rather than an optimisation.|Endless waves with new bad ideas and increasingly absurd enemies.|Making defence funny without making it random is a delicate and rewarding design.|tower-defense,comedy,physics,levels",
"g403|Auto-Battler Bakery|Auto-Battler / Food|js|drag|pastel|Assemble a pastry team, then watch them fight a wedding order.|Build a team of bakers with abilities. Battles are orders that must be fulfilled under pressure.|The combat is production, which reframes the genre entirely.|Endless orders with new bakery classes and synergies.|Reframing combat as production is a clever and very extensible idea.|auto-battler,strategy,food,levels",
"g404|Roguelike Post Office|Roguelike / Comedy|js|tap|paper|Deliver mail through a procedurally generated town where the addresses keep changing.|Each run is a new town with new routes, hazards and residents. Deliveries unlock permanent upgrades.|The mundane frame makes the roguelike loop feel human rather than epic.|Endless runs with new towns, weather and delivery types.|A roguelike about delivering mail is a strong, warm and funny premise.|roguelike,strategy,comedy,procedural",
"g405|Hex Garden|Strategy / Hex|js|drag|watercolor|Plant on hexes, and each plant changes the rules of its neighbours.|Every plant modifies adjacent tiles. Placing one changes the value of everything around it.|Local rule modification creates deep emergent strategy from simple pieces.|Endless generated hex maps with new plant families.|Local rule modification is one of the deepest simple mechanics available.|strategy,hex,emergence,levels",
"g406|Siege of Sandcastles|Strategy / Physics|js|drag|pastel|Lay siege to a sandcastle with a bucket and a tide table.|Build siege equipment from beach objects and time your assault with the tide.|The tide is a shared clock for both sides, which makes timing the core strategy.|Endless castles with new defences and tide schedules.|A strategy game where the environment is the timer is elegant and thematic.|strategy,physics,beach,levels",
"g407|Card Ladder|Strategy / Cards|js|drag|duotone|Cards can only be played on cards of a higher tier, so the ladder is the game.|Build ascending sequences. The board fills and the ladder must keep climbing.|A strict ascending constraint creates a tense, elegant puzzle-battler.|Endless ladders with new card families.|One strict rule plus a filling board is a proven and deep design.|strategy,cards,puzzle,levels",
"g408|Draft the Dungeon|Roguelike / Drafting|js|tap|voxel|You draft the dungeon before you enter it, and so does your enemy.|Both sides alternate drafting rooms, traps and monsters into a shared dungeon, then you run it.|Drafting your own challenge and then surviving it is a brilliant inversion.|Endless drafts with new room types and enemy behaviours.|Drafting the level you then play is a strong and original roguelike structure.|roguelike,drafting,strategy,levels",
"g409|Minion Middle Management|Strategy / Comedy|js|drag|clay|You are the middle manager between an evil overlord and a workforce of minions.|Assign minions to tasks, manage morale, and translate the overlord's absurd demands into achievable work.|Corporate satire as a strategy game with real systems is genuinely funny and deep.|Endless campaigns with new overlords and workforce problems.|Corporate satire with real management systems is a strong and funny premise.|strategy,comedy,management,levels",
"g410|Turret Tetris|Tower Defense / Puzzle|js|drag|vector|Turrets are tetromino shapes. Fit them into the map or you cannot place them.|Space is the constraint, not money. You must pack defences into a limited footprint.|Combining packing puzzles with tower defence is a genuinely new hybrid.|Endless maps with new footprints and enemy paths.|A packing constraint on tower placement is a clever and novel idea.|tower-defense,puzzle,spatial,levels",
"g411|Path of Least Resistance|Strategy / Maze|js|drag|mono|Enemies always take the shortest path. You design the path, not the walls.|Place obstacles to route enemies through your defences. The pathfinding is the puzzle.|Designing against pathfinding is a rich and underused strategy space.|Endless maps with new pathfinding rules and enemy types.|Designing for an algorithm rather than a player is a fascinating design space.|strategy,maze,pathfinding,levels",
"g412|Warlord Accountant|Strategy / Comedy|js|tap|paper|Every conquest must balance the books. Your army is a spreadsheet with swords.|Manage supply, payroll and morale while expanding. Overextension is bankruptcy.|Making logistics the actual game is a mature and rare strategy design.|Endless campaigns with new economies and rivals.|Logistics as the core of a strategy game is a mature and rewarding choice.|strategy,logistics,comedy,levels",
"g413|Spell Spelling|Strategy / Words|js|typing|ink|To cast a spell you must spell it correctly, and the spells are real words with real meanings.|Type the spell name to cast it. Longer, rarer words are more powerful but harder to type under pressure.|Vocabulary becomes the spellbook, which is a delightful fusion.|Endless spell lists with new languages and word classes.|Making vocabulary the magic system is a strong and elegant fusion.|strategy,words,typing,levels",
"g414|Battle Chef Duel|Strategy / Food|js|drag|clay|Two chefs compete to satisfy one diner whose tastes change mid-meal.|Both players cook for a shared diner. The diner's preferences shift based on what they have eaten.|A shared, adaptive objective makes competition indirect and strategic.|Endless diners with new preference models.|An adaptive shared objective is a sophisticated and interesting competitive design.|strategy,food,versus,adaptive",
"g415|Formation Farmer|Strategy / Positioning|js|drag|pastel|You arrange crops in formations that fight pests like an army.|Different crops have abilities and adjacency bonuses. Pests attack in waves.|Farming as a tactics game is a fresh and charming reframe.|Endless seasons with new crops, pests and formations.|Reframing farming as tactics is a strong and very extensible idea.|strategy,farming,tactics,levels",
"g416|Empire of Paperwork|Strategy / Bureaucracy|js|drag|mono|Your empire expands by filing forms. Each new territory adds administrative load.|Expansion increases paperwork, which reduces capacity, which requires more expansion to fund.|A deliberately self-defeating economy that the player must escape is a brilliant satire.|Endless empires with new bureaucratic systems.|A strategy game whose antagonist is its own administration is a great joke and a real system.|strategy,satire,systems,levels",
"g417|Scout & Sabotage|Strategy / Hidden Info|js|drag|duotone|You cannot see the map. You can only see what your scouts report, and scouts lie.|Send scouts to reveal terrain. Their reports have errors that grow with distance.|Information quality as a resource is a mature and rarely used strategy mechanic.|Endless maps with new scout reliability curves.|Unreliable information is a rich and realistic strategy space.|strategy,fog-of-war,information,levels",
"g418|Card Counter's Dilemma|Strategy / Cards|js|tap|terminal|You can see the deck. The problem is that so can your opponent, and they know you can.|Perfect information card game where both players see everything and must out-think each other.|Perfect information removes luck and makes it purely about reading intent.|Endless decks with new card sets.|Perfect-information card design is rare and deeply strategic.|strategy,cards,perfect-information,levels",
"g419|Territory Tiles|Strategy / Area Control|js|drag|isometric|Place tiles to claim territory, but tiles you place also help your opponent.|Every placement has shared consequences, so expansion is always a negotiation with the board.|Shared consequences make area control tense without direct conflict.|Endless boards with new tile sets.|Making every move help your rival is an elegant tension generator.|strategy,area-control,tiles,levels",
"g420|Roguelike Elevator|Roguelike / Descent|js|tap|voxel|A dungeon that is a single elevator shaft going down forever.|Each floor is a small room. You choose whether to descend or stay and loot, and the elevator never comes back up.|Irreversible descent gives a roguelike genuine momentum.|Endless floors with new room types and hazards.|A one-way descent structure is a strong and simple roguelike frame.|roguelike,descent,procedural,endless",
"g421|Boss Rush Builder|Strategy / Boss|js|drag|neon|You build the boss, then you have to beat it.|Design a boss from a parts library, then fight it. The game remembers your design and reuses it.|Designing your own antagonist is a remarkable and rare idea.|Endless bosses, and a shared library of other players' bosses.|Letting players design their own enemies creates infinite content and personal challenge.|strategy,boss,creative,sharing",
"g422|Deck of Emotions|Strategy / Cards|js|drag|watercolor|Your cards are feelings. Playing them changes what your opponent can play.|Emotional states modify the rules: anger unlocks power but blocks defence, calm enables precision.|Emotional state as a resource system is a genuinely original design.|Endless emotional card sets and interactions.|Modelling emotion as a game system is ambitious and original.|strategy,cards,emotion,levels",
"g423|Strategic Sourdough|Strategy / Timing|js|tap|clay|Your starter is a living resource that must be fed, and it is also your army.|The starter's health determines your power. Neglecting it weakens everything.|A living, decaying resource base creates constant low-level attention demands.|Endless weeks with new feeding schedules and competitions.|A resource that requires ongoing care is a great way to create daily engagement honestly.|strategy,food,care,levels",
"g424|Wargame of Manners|Strategy / Etiquette|js|tap|ink|A wargame where every aggressive move costs you social standing.|Attacking is powerful but rude. Politeness is a resource that gates your options.|Making etiquette a strategic resource is a wonderful and very British idea.|Endless campaigns with new social rules.|Turning social convention into a game resource is a genuinely original design.|strategy,satire,social,levels",
"g425|Chess Variant Generator|Strategy / Chess|js|drag|mono|The game generates a new chess variant, explains it, then makes you play it.|Every run uses a generated rule change (new piece, new movement, new win condition).|Generated variants give chess infinite replayability without any new content authoring.|Endless variants with a shared daily variant for everyone.|Procedural rule generation applied to chess is a rich and largely unexplored space.|strategy,chess,generated,daily",
"g426|Go Variant Generator|Strategy / Go|js|tap|duotone|Same as chess variants, but for Go, where small rule changes have enormous effects.|Generated rule variations: capture rules, scoring rules, board topology.|Go's simplicity means small changes produce radically different games, which is perfect for generation.|Endless variants with a daily shared board.|Rule generation on a simple game produces enormous variety.|strategy,go,generated,daily",
"g427|Draft the Weather|Strategy / Environment|js|drag|watercolor|You draft the weather for the coming week, and so does your rival.|Both players draft weather cards that affect a shared map. Weather determines what is possible.|Weather as a draftable strategic resource is a fresh and thematic idea.|Endless weeks with new weather systems and maps.|Drafting the environment rather than the units is a genuinely new strategic axis.|strategy,drafting,weather,versus",
"g428|Tower of Whispers|Strategy / Information|js|tap|ink|Information travels up a tower and gets distorted. You must act on what arrives.|You receive reports from the top of the tower, but each floor alters them. You must infer the truth.|Information degradation as a core mechanic is rich and unusual.|Endless towers with new distortion rules.|Modelling information decay as a strategy mechanic is genuinely original.|strategy,information,deduction,levels",
"g429|Loyalty Cards|Deckbuilder / Allies|js|drag|paper|Your cards are people, and they have opinions about being played.|Each ally card has a loyalty value that decreases when used. Disloyal allies defect.|Managing relationships inside a deck is a beautiful and rare mechanic.|Endless ally sets with new loyalty dynamics.|Making deck cards have feelings is a wonderful twist on the genre.|deckbuilder,strategy,relationships,levels",
"g430|Resource Roulette|Strategy / Risk|js|tap|neon|You choose how much risk to take on every resource gain. More risk, more reward, more ruin.|Each turn you set a risk level. Outcomes are probabilistic but with visible odds.|Making risk an explicit dial rather than a hidden modifier is honest and strategic.|Endless rounds with new risk structures.|Explicit risk dials make probability transparent and strategic.|strategy,risk,probability,levels",
"g431|Battle of Bureaucrats|Strategy / Satire|js|tap|mono|Two departments fight for budget. The weapons are memos and the battlefield is a meeting.|Deploy arguments as cards. Win by exhausting the other department's patience.|Office politics as a tactics game is funny, relatable and cheap to build.|Endless departments with new argument types.|A deeply relatable satire with real strategy underneath.|strategy,satire,cards,comedy",
"g432|Rogue Ledger|Roguelike / Economy|js|drag|terminal|A roguelike where your health is your bank balance and your enemies are expenses.|Every encounter costs money. You survive by earning. Death is bankruptcy.|Making the economy the health bar is an elegant and unusual design.|Endless runs with new expense types and income sources.|Reframing survival as solvency is a strong, original roguelike idea.|roguelike,economy,strategy,levels",
"g433|Cardboard Kingdom|Strategy / Craft|js|drag|paper|Your kingdom is made of cardboard. Rain is the apocalypse.|Build structures from cardboard that must survive weather. Each turn brings new conditions.|Material fragility as a strategic constraint is charming and readable.|Endless weather systems with new building materials.|Fragility plus weather creates a strategy game with real texture.|strategy,craft,weather,levels",
"g434|Dice Garden|Strategy / Dice|js|drag|watercolor|Dice are seeds. Plant them, and they grow into the numbers they rolled.|Rolled values become plants that produce that many resources per turn. Placement determines yield.|Making randomness into a garden is a lovely and strategic idea.|Endless seasons with new dice types and soil conditions.|Turning randomness into cultivation is a beautiful reframe.|strategy,dice,growth,levels",
"g435|Luckless|Strategy / No-Randomness|js|drag|mono|A card game with absolutely no randomness. Every game is decided purely by decisions.|Perfect information, deterministic rules, no shuffling. Every loss is a lesson.|Removing luck entirely makes a game brutal and instructive.|Endless scenarios with new deterministic rule sets.|Zero-randomness design is a bold and instructive choice.|strategy,deterministic,puzzle,levels",
"g436|Perfect Information Duel|Strategy / Duel|js|tap|duotone|Both players see everything: hands, deck order, intentions. Only choices remain.|A duel with total transparency. The skill is in reading your opponent's reasoning.|Total transparency removes all excuses and makes the game purely psychological.|Endless matchups with new rule sets.|Complete transparency is the purest form of strategic competition.|strategy,perfect-information,versus,levels",
"g437|Fog of War Puzzle|Strategy / Puzzle|js|drag|ink|A puzzle where the map is hidden and revealing it is part of the solution.|You can only see adjacent tiles. Exploring costs moves, and the goal requires a specific route.|Reconnaissance as a puzzle constraint is fresh and tense.|Endless generated maps with new goal types.|Combining fog of war with puzzle design is a genuinely new hybrid.|strategy,puzzle,fog-of-war,levels",
"g438|Supply Line|Strategy / Logistics|js|drag|paper|Your army is only as good as the line that feeds it. The line is the game.|Draw supply routes across a map. Enemies cut lines rather than fight battles.|Logistics as the entire strategic content is a mature and rare design.|Endless campaigns with new terrain and threats.|A strategy game where the only real weapon is logistics is deeply interesting.|strategy,logistics,levels,planning",
"g439|Morale Machine|Strategy / Psychology|js|drag|clay|Units do not have health. They have morale, and morale is contagious.|Units flee based on nearby morale. Panic spreads, and courage spreads too.|Contagious morale is a rich, emergent system that mirrors real battle psychology.|Endless battles with new morale dynamics.|Contagion mechanics produce emergent behaviour that is endlessly interesting.|strategy,morale,emergence,levels",
"g440|Siege Psychology|Strategy / Negotiation|js|tap|ink|You can end any siege by negotiating. The question is whether your side will accept the terms.|Battles are fought, but the real game is managing your own side's expectations.|Making internal politics the constraint on external strategy is sophisticated.|Endless sieges with new factions and demands.|Internal politics as the strategic constraint is a mature and rare design.|strategy,negotiation,politics,levels",
"g441|Card Evolution|Deckbuilder / Growth|js|drag|neon|Cards level up by being played in specific combinations, permanently changing your deck.|Cards that survive and succeed evolve new abilities based on how they were used.|Decks that record their own history is a beautiful and rare mechanic.|Endless runs with persistent deck evolution across runs.|Persistent evolution across runs is a strong roguelike meta-progression idea.|deckbuilder,roguelike,evolution,persistent",
"g442|Deck Degradation|Deckbuilder / Decay|js|drag|duotone|Cards wear out as you play them. Your best card will eventually tear.|Cards have durability. Using them is necessary and destructive.|Forcing players to destroy their own best tools is a brilliant tension.|Endless runs with new durability rules.|Making the player destroy their own advantages is a strong and unusual mechanic.|deckbuilder,decay,strategy,levels",
"g443|Boss Deck|Strategy / Boss|js|drag|voxel|The boss is a deck of cards, and you can see it. You must build against what is coming.|Full knowledge of the boss's deck means the game is a construction puzzle rather than a gamble.|Known threats make deckbuilding a genuine planning exercise.|Endless bosses with new deck compositions.|Perfect knowledge of the threat makes deckbuilding a real puzzle.|strategy,deckbuilder,boss,levels",
"g444|Arena of Small Numbers|Strategy / Math|js|drag|terminal|All values are between 1 and 5. Every decision matters enormously.|A tactics game with tiny numbers, so each point of damage is a major event.|Small numbers make strategy legible and every choice consequential.|Endless arenas with new unit sets.|Tiny number ranges are a great way to make strategy readable on a small screen.|strategy,tactics,minimal,levels",
"g445|Draft & Ban|Strategy / Competitive|js|tap|neon|Before the match, you draft what you will use and ban what you fear.|A draft phase determines the match before it begins, and the draft is the real contest.|Making the pre-match a game in itself is a strong competitive structure.|Endless card pools with new draft formats.|The draft as the primary competitive act is a proven and deep design.|strategy,drafting,versus,levels",
"g446|Puzzle Battler|Strategy / Puzzle|js|drag|vector|Your attacks are puzzle solutions. Solve faster to hit harder.|Each turn presents a small puzzle. How quickly you solve it determines damage.|Fusing puzzle-solving with combat creates a hybrid that rewards both skills.|Endless battles with new puzzle types.|Timed puzzles as combat mechanics is a strong and very mobile-friendly fusion.|strategy,puzzle,combat,levels",
"g447|Roguelike Shopkeeper|Roguelike / Economy|js|drag|clay|You are the shopkeeper. Heroes come to buy, and they die with your stock.|Equip heroes and watch them die. Their failure reveals what your shop should stock.|Learning from customer deaths is a darkly funny and strategic loop.|Endless runs with new hero types and demand patterns.|A roguelike where you are the merchant rather than the hero is a great inversion.|roguelike,economy,comedy,levels",
"g448|Tactics in a Teacup|Strategy / Tactics|js|drag|pastel|A tactics game on a surface the size of a teacup.|Tiny grid, few units, enormous consequence per move.|Extreme spatial constraint makes tactics legible and deep.|Endless tiny maps with new unit sets.|Extreme constraint on a tactics game is a great way to make it mobile-native.|strategy,tactics,minimal,levels",
"g449|Empire of Habits|Strategy / Real-life|js|tap|watercolor|Your empire grows only when you do your real-world habits.|Each completed habit adds a turn. The game runs on your actual behaviour.|A strategy game that runs on your real habits is a genuine life-integration idea.|Endless campaigns that advance at the pace of your real life.|Real-life integration with a strategy game is a powerful and honest hook.|strategy,habits,real-world,persistent",
"g450|Final Strategy|Strategy / Meta|js|drag|neon|Every fifty battles, the game asks you to design the next one, then plays it against you.|You design a scenario from your unlocked pieces, then the AI plays it against you.|Designing your own final exam is a remarkable and personal climax.|Endless: a self-designed challenge every fifty battles.|Making the player author their own final boss is a brilliant meta structure.|strategy,meta,boss,milestones",
"g451|One Room, One Year|Narrative / Time|js|tap|watercolor|A single room, seen once a day for a year, and you must infer the story.|Each day you see the room's state. Objects move, accumulate and disappear. The narrative is never stated.|Environmental storytelling as the entire game is elegant and deeply engaging.|Endless: a new room and a new year each time you finish one.|Pure environmental inference is a mature and powerful narrative form.|narrative,story,minimal,inference",
"g452|The House Remembers|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|duotone|Every object in the house has a memory of what happened near it.|Tap objects to hear their memory. Contradictions between objects reveal the truth.|Multiple unreliable narrators embedded in furniture is a wonderful idea.|Endless houses with new memory networks.|Distributed unreliable narration is a sophisticated narrative mechanic.|narrative,horror,mystery,levels",
"g453|Voicemail Ghost|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|mono|You inherit a phone full of voicemails from someone who is still leaving them.|Messages arrive over real days. Each one reveals more and asks you to respond.|Real-time delivery makes a narrative game genuinely unsettling.|Endless: new voicemail stories, each over several days.|Real-time narrative delivery is a strong and rarely used format.|narrative,horror,real-time,audio",
"g454|Neighbour Watch|Narrative / Mystery|js|tap|duotone|Watch a neighbour's window for a month. Decide whether to intervene.|Each night you see a fragment. You can act or not, and both have consequences.|Moral agency with incomplete information is a powerful narrative design.|Endless windows with new stories and moral dilemmas.|Incomplete information plus moral choice is a strong narrative combination.|narrative,mystery,morality,levels",
"g455|Elevator Confessions|Narrative / Audio|js|tap|mono|Strangers tell you things in an elevator because they will never see you again.|Each ride is a short confession. You can respond or stay silent, and both matter.|Confession as a narrative unit is intimate and endlessly generative.|Endless rides with new confessions and response consequences.|A simple, intimate narrative frame that scales to hundreds of stories.|narrative,audio,anthology,levels",
"g456|Last Message|Narrative / Drama|js|typing|ink|You have one message left and no idea how it will be received.|Write a message to a character. The game responds based on tone analysis, not keywords.|Tone-sensitive responses make writing feel genuinely interactive.|Endless scenarios with new relationships and stakes.|Tone-based narrative response is a genuinely novel interaction model.|narrative,writing,emotion,levels",
"g457|Static|Narrative / Horror|js|drag|mono|Tune a radio through a night of static, finding fragments of a broadcast that should not exist.|Drag the dial. Signals fade in and out, and the story is assembled from fragments you happen to catch.|Tuning as narrative discovery is beautiful and tension-filled.|Endless nights with new broadcasts and signal patterns.|Tuning as a narrative mechanic is elegant and atmospheric.|narrative,horror,audio,discovery",
"g458|The Shape in the Fog|Narrative / Horror|js|drag|duotone|You can only see three metres. Something is out there, and it moves when you do not look.|Navigate by sound and inference. The thing's behaviour is generated from your own movement patterns.|An antagonist that learns your habits is genuinely frightening.|Endless nights with new behaviour models.|Adaptive horror is far more effective than scripted scares.|narrative,horror,adaptive,atmosphere",
"g459|3AM|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|mono|A game designed to be played at 3am, and it knows what time it is.|The game's content changes based on the actual time you play it. Night content is different.|Real-time awareness creates a genuinely personal horror experience.|Endless nights, each different from the last.|Time-aware content is a simple mechanic with enormous atmospheric effect.|narrative,horror,real-time,atmosphere",
"g460|Footsteps Behind|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|ink|You hear footsteps behind you. They match your pace exactly.|You walk through a corridor. The footsteps follow. Stopping is the only way to learn what is behind you.|Matching pace is a beautifully simple tension generator.|Endless corridors with new pursuers.|Pace-matching as a horror mechanic is simple, effective and rarely used.|narrative,horror,tension,endless",
"g461|The Quiet Floor|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|duotone|A hospital floor where all the patients are asleep and one of them should not be.|You are a night nurse. You must check on patients and notice what is wrong.|Mundane work plus subtle wrongness is the most effective horror structure.|Endless nights with new patients and anomalies.|Routine as horror scaffolding is a proven and powerful design.|narrative,horror,routine,mystery",
"g462|Mirror Delay|Narrative / Horror|js|drag|mono|Your reflection moves a fraction of a second late, and each day the delay grows.|You interact with a mirror that is increasingly out of sync. The delay reveals things.|A slowly worsening anomaly is a great long-form horror structure.|Endless days with new mirror behaviour.|Incremental wrongness over time is deeply unsettling.|narrative,horror,time,atmosphere",
"g463|The Guest Book|Narrative / Mystery|js|typing|paper|A hotel guest book spanning eighty years, and one name appears in every decade.|Read entries and find connections. You can write your own entry, and it becomes part of the book.|Contributing to the artefact makes the player part of the mystery.|Endless books with new threads to unravel.|Player contributions to a persistent artefact are a strong narrative hook.|narrative,mystery,persistent,writing",
"g464|Photograph of a Stranger|Narrative / Mystery|js|drag|duotone|You find a photograph in a second-hand book and must reconstruct the life in it.|Use fragments, dates and details in the photo to piece together a biography.|A found-object premise with real investigative structure is compelling.|Endless photographs with new lives to reconstruct.|Found-object investigation is a strong, low-cost narrative frame.|narrative,mystery,investigation,levels",
"g465|The Night Shift|Narrative / Drama|js|tap|mono|A petrol station at night. Everyone who stops has something wrong.|Serve customers, listen, and decide whether to intervene in their lives.|Small interactions with large implications is a beautiful narrative design.|Endless nights with new customers and stories.|Episodic encounters with moral weight is a proven narrative structure.|narrative,drama,episodic,levels",
"g466|Lighthouse Alone|Narrative / Solitude|js|tap|duotone|Six months alone with a logbook, and something in the water.|Keep the light, write the log, and record what you see. Your log entries become the story.|The player authors the record, which makes the story theirs.|Endless seasons with new events and interpretations.|Player-authored documentation as narrative is a strong and rare idea.|narrative,solitude,atmosphere,writing",
"g467|Signal Lost|Narrative / Sci-Fi|js|drag|neon|A deep space station has gone quiet. You have the last twelve hours of telemetry.|Reconstruct events from telemetry data by scrubbing and cross-referencing.|Investigating through data rather than dialogue is a fresh narrative mechanic.|Endless stations with new telemetry sets.|Data forensics as narrative is genuinely original and very replayable.|narrative,sci-fi,investigation,data",
"g468|The Long Hallway|Narrative / Horror|js|tap|mono|A hallway that gets longer each time you look away.|You walk. The hallway extends. The rooms you pass change, and the changes are the story.|An infinite corridor where progress is measured in understanding, not distance.|Endless corridors with new room sequences.|Spatial impossibility as narrative structure is elegant and unsettling.|narrative,horror,space,atmosphere",
"g469|Room 0|Narrative / Mystery|js|tap|ink|A hotel with no room zero, and a key that opens it.|Each attempt to find room zero reveals more about the hotel and its guests.|A single impossible object drives the entire narrative, which is very efficient.|Endless hotels with new impossible features.|One impossible object as narrative engine is efficient and compelling.|narrative,mystery,levels,atmosphere",
"g470|The Tape|Narrative / Horror|js|drag|mono|A cassette tape with forty minutes of recording and a lot of silence.|Scrub the tape. The silences contain more information than the speech, if you listen closely.|Silence as narrative content is a bold and effective choice.|Endless tapes with new recordings.|Making silence the payload is a genuinely bold narrative design.|narrative,horror,audio,discovery",
"g471|Barometer|Narrative / Weather Horror|js|tap|duotone|The pressure is dropping and it has been dropping for eleven days.|You monitor instruments. The readings are the story. The weather is wrong.|Instrumentation as narrative is unusual, clinical and very effective.|Endless weather events with new readings.|Making instruments the narrator is a fresh and chilling idea.|narrative,horror,data,atmosphere",
"g472|The Garden Grows|Narrative / Drama|js|drag|watercolor|You tend a garden that a missing person planted, and it tells you where they went.|Each plant reveals a clue when it blooms. You must decide what to plant next.|Gardening as investigation is gentle, beautiful and structurally sound.|Endless gardens with new stories.|Combining cultivation with investigation is a lovely and original pairing.|narrative,drama,gardening,mystery",
"g473|Inheritance|Narrative / Drama|js|tap|paper|You inherit a house and everything in it, including problems you did not cause.|Sort through belongings, each with a decision attached. Your choices compound.|An inheritance as a decision space is emotionally rich and endlessly generative.|Endless houses with new legacies.|A house full of decisions is a strong and human narrative structure.|narrative,drama,decisions,levels",
"g474|The Last Customer|Narrative / Drama|js|tap|clay|A shop closing forever, and one customer who will not leave.|Serve them, talk to them, or ask them to go. The conversation is the whole game.|A single conversation with real stakes is a powerful and cheap narrative design.|Endless shops with new customers.|One conversation as the entire game is bold, cheap and potentially beautiful.|narrative,drama,dialogue,minimal",
"g475|Paper Boat|Narrative / Grief|js|drag|watercolor|Fold paper boats and send them downstream, each carrying something you cannot say.|Write a message, fold it, and release it. Boats accumulate downstream over time.|An accumulating record of unsaid things is emotionally powerful.|Endless rivers with accumulating messages.|A game about unsaid things is emotionally mature and rare.|narrative,grief,zen,writing",
"g476|Letters to No One|Narrative / Writing|js|typing|paper|Write letters to a person who will never read them, and the game replies as them anyway.|Each letter gets a response generated from your own previous letters, mirroring your language back.|An echo that sounds like a person is haunting and beautiful.|Endless letters with evolving responses.|Mirroring the player's own words back is a genuinely striking narrative device.|narrative,writing,emotion,generated",
"g477|The Museum of Small Regrets|Narrative / Anthology|js|tap|duotone|Every exhibit is a small regret, and you must arrange them into a life.|Read exhibits and place them in chronological order to reconstruct a person.|Curation as biography is a strong and elegant narrative frame.|Endless museums with new lives.|Making curation the narrative act is a mature and original design.|narrative,anthology,curation,levels",
"g478|Twenty Years of Tuesdays|Narrative / Time|js|tap|paper|Every scene is a Tuesday, twenty years apart, and the gaps are the story.|You see only Tuesdays. What happened in between must be inferred from changes.|Extreme temporal ellipsis as a narrative device is bold and effective.|Endless: twenty years of a new life each time.|Making absence the narrative content is a sophisticated and rare choice.|narrative,time,inference,levels",
"g479|The Cartographer's Daughter|Narrative / Adventure|js|drag|ink|Your father mapped a coastline that does not exist. You must find it.|Navigate using an impossible map, and the map's errors are clues.|A wrong map as the central mystery is a beautiful narrative device.|Endless maps with new errors to interpret.|Making the map the mystery is an elegant and original narrative frame.|narrative,adventure,maps,mystery",
"g480|A Year in One Street|Narrative / Community|js|tap|isometric|One street, twelve households, one year, and every choice ripples.|You influence small decisions. Over a year, the consequences compound across neighbours.|Compounding social consequences over a year is a rich simulation narrative.|Endless streets with new households.|A small cast with compounding consequences is a strong and efficient narrative design.|narrative,community,simulation,levels",
"g481|The Bench|Narrative / Observation|js|tap|watercolor|A park bench, four seasons, and everyone who sits on it.|You observe conversations and can leave small notes that change outcomes.|Minimal intervention with visible consequences is a gentle, powerful design.|Endless years with new sitters.|Small interventions with visible effects is a mature and kind narrative design.|narrative,observation,zen,levels",
"g482|Postcards from a Flood|Narrative / Disaster|js|tap|duotone|Postcards arrive from a town that is slowly disappearing under water.|Each postcard is dated and describes a place. You must decide whether to go.|A slow disaster told through mundane correspondence is devastating and efficient.|Endless towns with new disasters.|Mundane documentation of catastrophe is a powerful narrative technique.|narrative,disaster,epistolary,levels",
"g483|The Sound of Home|Narrative / Memory|js|tap|mono|Reconstruct a childhood home from the sounds you remember.|Place sounds in a floor plan. Each sound unlocks a memory fragment.|Sound as spatial memory is a beautiful and rarely used narrative device.|Endless homes with new sound sets.|Building memory from audio is a strong and unusual narrative mechanic.|narrative,memory,audio,levels",
"g484|The Recipe Book|Narrative / Food|js|drag|clay|A recipe book with missing pages, and the missing recipes are the story.|Cook from fragments. The dishes reveal family history as you reconstruct them.|Cooking as archaeology is a warm and structurally elegant narrative.|Endless books with new families.|Reconstruction through cooking is a lovely and original narrative frame.|narrative,food,mystery,levels",
"g485|Grandfather's Radio|Narrative / Memory|js|drag|mono|Tune a radio to the stations your grandfather listened to, and hear his life.|Each station is a decade. Tuning between them reveals his history through what he heard.|Tuning as time travel is elegant and atmospheric.|Endless radios with new lives.|A single object as a time machine is efficient and beautiful.|narrative,memory,audio,time",
"g486|The Last Train|Narrative / Farewell|js|tap|duotone|A night train, six passengers, and everyone is leaving something.|Each carriage holds a conversation. You choose how much to listen.|A contained journey with a fixed ending is a strong narrative structure.|Endless journeys with new passengers.|A journey with a known end is a powerful dramatic structure.|narrative,drama,journey,levels",
"g487|Tide Tables|Narrative / Nature|js|drag|watercolor|A coastal town's tide tables over fifty years, and the sea is winning.|Read the tables and see the town change. You can intervene, but only slowly.|Data as narrative is unusual, beautiful and quietly devastating.|Endless coastlines with new datasets.|Making a dataset the narrator is a bold and effective idea.|narrative,nature,data,levels",
"g488|The Orchard|Narrative / Generations|js|drag|pastel|Plant trees that will outlive you, and see who eats the fruit.|Each tree takes decades. You play across generations, and the story is what changes.|Multi-generational time scales in a game are rare and powerful.|Endless generations with new orchards.|Playing across generations is an ambitious and rewarding narrative scope.|narrative,generations,nature,levels",
"g489|Small Kindnesses|Narrative / Kindness|js|tap|pastel|A day in a city, and every small kindness you can afford to give.|You have limited time and money. Each kindness helps one person and costs you something.|Scarcity makes kindness meaningful rather than trivial.|Endless days with new cities and people.|Making kindness costly is what makes a kindness game meaningful.|narrative,kindness,scarcity,levels",
"g490|The Apartment Above|Narrative / Neighbours|js|tap|duotone|You hear everything through the ceiling, and you have to decide what to do about it.|Sound-based neighbour narrative with moral choices. You never see them.|Sound-only relationships are intimate, mysterious and cheap to produce.|Endless apartments with new upstairs lives.|An unseen neighbour as narrative subject is a strong and unusual choice.|narrative,neighbours,audio,morality",
"g491|Step Garden|Sensor / Real-world|js|shake|watercolor|Your real steps grow a garden. Walking is the only way to water it.|The pedometer drives growth. Plants mature based on real distance walked.|A step counter that grows something is a genuinely motivating fitness hook.|Endless gardens with new species and biomes.|Turning exercise into cultivation is one of the most reliable real-world game hooks.|sensor,steps,fitness,garden",
"g492|Barometer Run|Sensor / Weather|js|tilt|mono|The game changes based on real atmospheric pressure. Storms make it harder.|Pressure readings alter the game's physics and difficulty in real time.|Real weather as a difficulty modifier is a genuinely novel idea.|Endless runs that are different every day.|Real sensor data as a difficulty modifier is fresh and memorable.|sensor,weather,real-world,endless",
"g493|Magnetometer Treasure|Sensor / Metal|js|drag|neon|Your phone's magnetometer detects metal. Find the treasure hidden in the room.|The compass/magnetometer reading guides you toward metal objects. The room is the level.|Using the magnetometer as a metal detector is a genuinely delightful idea.|Endless hunts in new locations.|Turning a phone sensor into a treasure hunt is memorable and physical.|sensor,magnetometer,treasure,real-world",
"g494|Gyroscope Maze|Sensor / Motion|js|tilt|vector|The maze rotates with your phone. Gravity is the only force.|Tilt the phone to roll a ball through a maze that exists in three dimensions.|Physical rotation as the control is intuitive and tactile.|Endless mazes with new three-dimensional layouts.|Physical device rotation as a control scheme is underused and satisfying.|sensor,gyroscope,maze,physical",
"g495|Microphone Echo|Sensor / Audio|js|voice|mono|Clap in a room and the game measures the echo to build a level.|The microphone analyses the room's acoustic response and generates geometry from it.|Your actual room becomes the level. That is a remarkable idea.|Endless rooms, each generating a different level.|Room acoustics as level generation is an extraordinary and original idea.|sensor,audio,room-scan,generated",
"g496|Camera Colour Hunt|Sensor / Camera|js|camera|neon|Find an object in the real world that matches a target colour exactly.|The camera samples colours. You must find real objects matching the target within a tolerance.|A real-world colour hunt is simple, physical and genuinely fun.|Endless colour targets with new tolerances.|A camera game that sends you into the world is simple and delightful.|sensor,camera,colour,real-world",
"g497|Light Sensor Shadow|Sensor / Light|js|drag|duotone|The game is played with your finger covering the light sensor, and light is a resource.|Cover and uncover the sensor to control the game. Darkness and light are resources.|Using the ambient light sensor as a control is genuinely novel.|Endless levels with new light mechanics.|A sensor nobody uses as a primary control is a strong differentiator.|sensor,light,physical,levels",
"g498|Pressure|Sensor / Barometer|js|tap|mono|A game that runs over days, and the weather changes the story.|The barometer drives narrative events. Storms bring plot, clear skies bring calm.|Weather-driven narrative is slow, ambient and genuinely unique.|Endless days with weather-driven events.|Letting real weather drive narrative is a beautiful and rare design.|sensor,weather,narrative,ambient",
"g499|Compass Quest|Sensor / Direction|js|drag|ink|The game knows which way you are facing. Quests require you to face specific directions.|Turn in the real world to aim, navigate or unlock. The compass is the controller.|Directional puzzles in real space are physical and memorable.|Endless quests with new directional requirements.|Using real-world orientation as a puzzle input is genuinely original.|sensor,compass,real-world,quests",
"g500|Final Sense|Sensor / Meta|js|shake|neon|Every fifty levels, the game uses a different phone sensor you have never played with before.|Each milestone unlocks a new sensor-based mechanic, from barometer to magnetometer.|A game that progressively reveals your device's capabilities is genuinely surprising.|Endless: a new sensor mechanic every fifty levels, cycling through combinations.|Treating the phone as a sensor array rather than a screen is an inspiring design philosophy.|sensor,meta,discovery,milestones"
